					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Check_Content</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Universal method:
1. In the omnibox (address bar) type "chrome:// policy".
2. If "DevToolsGenAiSettings" is not displayed under the "Policy Name" column or it is not set to "2" under the "Policy Value" column, this is a finding.

Windows method:
1. Start "regedit".
2. Navigate to "HKLM\Software\Policies\Google\Chrome\".
3. If the "DevToolsGenAiSettings" value name does not exist or its value data is not set to "2", this is a finding.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA>
				</STIG_DATA>
				<STIG_DATA>
					<VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Fix_Text</VULN_ATTRIBUTE>
					<ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Windows group policy:
